00:01:21.068 --> 00:01:21.802
voters, move them in

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:23.003
positioning with suburbanites?

00:01:23.771 --> 00:01:25.873
That doesn't appear to be the

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:26.940
case if you look at the last

00:01:27.207 --> 00:01:27.941
presidential and it does not

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:29.176
appear to be the case if you

00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:30.811
look at the most recent midterm

00:01:31.078 --> 00:01:31.245
election.

00:01:31.512 --> 00:01:32.179
That is a concern that many in

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:33.380
the party, including donors,

00:01:33.647 --> 00:01:34.782
including other strategists,

00:01:35.048 --> 00:01:35.883
and even those working with

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.818
some of the folks who are not

00:01:38.085 --> 00:01:38.819
trump supporters saying, we

00:01:39.086 --> 00:01:39.987
want to win, and yes, we like

00:01:40.254 --> 00:01:41.155
trump, but is he the best

00:01:41.421 --> 00:01:42.156
person to help us get across

00:01:42.422 --> 00:01:43.056
that finish line?

00:01:43.791 --> 00:01:45.759
&gt;&gt; Yet, there's a huge

00:01:46.026 --> 00:01:46.794
disconnect right now between

00:01:46.794 --> 00:01:49.897
